### Rationale
This is a token-stationary, single-launch FP16x3 tcgen05 kernel for N ≤ 14,208 tokens, which covers every S and M row; larger rows fall back to r0 unchanged. **It has not been compiled or run.** Both probes timed out after 1800 s with no response, and the compile_b200 call was cut off when the session ended. Correctness, timing and the precision log are all still open, and the first thing to do next round is to compile it and run run_tests. The design follows E1. Phase 0 writes the hi/lo weight images and then waits on one grid counter. GEMM1 is swap-AB with all three products in one accumulator, and h stays in TMEM. Per-batch token counters reset themselves through the last CTA to depart. GEMM2's hi·hi product has its own accumulator, and the cross terms (scaled by 2^11) go into a second one. At t=96 that second accumulator reuses h block 0's columns. The h' tiles use an MN-major SW32 layout so that t=96 needs no padding. Hidden assumption: the SW32 descriptor encoding (layout 6, LBO = atom stride) is untested. If it is wrong, set HSW=128, which also switches the ring to 2 stages and fits.

