result:
### Rationale
I'm submitting the version that run_tests measured. Its code is unchanged from that test, apart from the new name. On the rented B200 it passed 14/14 workloads, and the projected portal score is 0.5325 ± 0.007, against 0.244 for r0. It is one cooperative tcgen05 FP16x3 launch with fp32 h kept in TMEM, for N ≤ 14,208 tokens; larger rows fall back to r0 unchanged. The success line was missed: 784 tokens ran in 21.0 µs (target 13) and 12,544 in 30–36 µs (target 21). The refutation criterion was not tested either, because the phase stamps were never built. At 784 tokens the MMA work is tiny, so roughly 19 µs looks like a fixed chain cost. My guess is the serial 3-stage, 16-unit weight ring plus the phase-0 grid wait. I wrote a follow-up with a ring depth computed from t (6 stages at t=16) but could not measure it: both run_tests calls timed out after 15 minutes because Modal had no B200 capacity. It goes into the findings as the next step.

